# rule.always.bear-every-self-review

> **a self review cannot be overridden. it is borne: as many honest reviews as it takes. no shortcuts.**

no overrule operation exists for self reviews, so never ask. the count is the WORK, never a budget. the guard holds you for no duration; `patience, friend` is a cue, not a gate.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| the count grows | more work found, not a guard defect; carry it |
| you would ask a human to waive one | no lever exists |
| `patience, friend` renders and you promise at once | it costs naught to ignore; that is why it tests you |
| the promise cleared on the first try | the design, not proof you reviewed enough |
| you repair the artifact mid-review | do it; no restart |
| `--as blocked` because the ladder feels long | length is not a wall |

test, per review: **"what did I find, and what did I settle?"** a repair, or a reasoned hold with evidence. neither → begin again.

blocker: a promise with no honest articulation · an articulation that names neither repair nor hold · a promise made because the guard would let it through · an ask to waive · a grown count reported as a malfunction · a self review batched.
